dfw (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * dfw enable refuses to run on a kernel without nft_meta_bridge or
    nf_conntrack_bridge, such as Raspberry Pi OS's, naming the missing
    modules, and dfw check reports them as an error.
  * dfw check lists each network's containers under it, and the rules one
    line per peer with the ports it reaches.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:19:24 +0100

dfw (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A running container that Docker fails to answer about keeps its rules,
    instead of being blocked and having its connections cut.

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:30:07 +0100

dfw (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: a bridge-level nftables firewall for the containers on
    chosen Docker networks, with allow rules in /etc/dfw/rules and
    /etc/dfw/rules.d. See README.md and dfw(8).

 -- dfw maintainers <lookap.dev@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
